import json
from pathlib import Path
root=Path.cwd();base=root/'reviews/split-audit-2026-10-15'
source=json.loads((base/'gemini/findings.json').read_text())['findings']
D={
'G-GEO-01':('accepted','P1','Independent numerical reproduction selects C (-752,-816),434 versus Python (-784,-816),422 with hut (56,-800). Recount at snapped center restores parity. The claimed 80-block within-cell displacement is unsupported and unnecessary to establish this defect.','Recount optional structures at the snapped center using exact half-open bounds; add an independent selection fixture.'),
'G-MEM-01':('accepted','P1','Two same-worker fixtures crash with SIGSEGV when allocation 34,35,or36 fails. Worker state is reused within a batch, not across native calls.','Allocate replacements into temporaries and publish pointers/capacities only after all required allocations succeed.'),
'G-MEM-02':('accepted','P1','One survivor fixture succeeds with cap 1,400,000 and peak requested live bytes 1,872,336, excluding SeedContext and allocator metadata. Retain earlier P1 severity because the documented resource bound is violated.','Route dynamic owned buffers through nb_alloc; preserve reuse and monotonic reservation semantics; define/reserve context cost.'),
'G-STORE-01':('accepted','P2','The (count,max(rowid)) signature cannot detect an in-place candidate UPDATE. Reproduced separately with temporary DB; earlier audit also observed score100 ->130 with UI remaining100.','Invalidate using a robust persistent revision or perform a bounded refresh; timestamps alone are not a proof of correctness.'),
'G-MEM-03':('accepted','P2','Popleft removes the current still-owned batch from pending before the early refill. Thus inflight=3 can own4 ranges. Existing targeted reproduction and current unchanged source agree; no end-to-end rerun performed.','Remove the early refill and replenish after the current batch has been committed and its native resources released.'),
'G-GEO-02':('accepted','validation gap','ReplayProvider intentionally supplies the C-selected center. This validates reconstruction, not independent center selection. Existing mandatory fixtures are independently evaluated, so calling all parity checks circular overstates the gap.','Keep replay checks; supplement independent selection fixtures with nonempty optional inventories and lattice boundary transitions.'),
'G-FFI-03':('duplicate','validation gap','NBFixture intentionally supplies empty optional inventories. This limits coverage; it is not truncation of production seed evidence. Consolidate with G-GEO-02; optional injection probe already demonstrates the missed bug.','Add a narrow optional-inventory test provider; do not expand the production ABI without a need.'),
'G-STORE-02':('unresolved','defensive hardening; production P1 not verified','Gemini callback deliberately recovers and reassigns the range on the same store between check and commit. This reproduces stale completion under that API interleaving, but production uses a single parent writer and an OS scan lock. A second scanner is independently rejected. Their probe shows completed_seeds=10 and the conflicting second commit rejected, not double-counting. No supported production interleaving supplied.','If lease operations are to support external reassignment, validate and update atomically inside a transaction, preserving idempotent retry behavior. Do not adopt the supplied invalid patch.'),
'G-STORE-03':('rejected','no verified production defect','complete_range is the trusted parent-owned compatibility path. A lease=None call bypasses an optional lease check by API design; workers do not receive writer authority. The probe invokes that trusted API manually.','No mandatory change; document the parent-owned contract if exposing a broader API.'),
'G-STORE-04':('rejected','no verified production defect','claim_range explicitly states Only the parent calls this. Simultaneous independent writer connections violate that contract and bypass scanner ownership. Gemini probe can return success even if no conflicting error occurs.','No multiwriter redesign justified for this production architecture.'),
'G-STORE-05':('accepted','P2','A deterministic two-second SIGINT-ignoring child holds pause_sweep under manager.lock; status blocks1.921s. Slow termination can delay other control requests.','Capture process ownership under lock, wait outside the lock, then revalidate the same process/generation before publishing state.'),
'G-GEO-03':('accepted','P3','README says20 per Bastion above three and shipwreck above five. Actual dynamic scoring gives Bastion counts2->3:+20,3->4:+0; shipwreck5->6:+0,6->7:+5. Monument second milestone remains+30.','Update the two README formulas to match approved active policy; do not alter scoring.'),
'G-MEM-04':('rejected','intentional behavior','The source explicitly documents deliberate monotonic reservation. It resets at each nb_run and any allocation error invalidates the batch. No permanent cross-batch poisoning was demonstrated.','Keep the reservation semantics; fix the bypass and unsafe capacity publication separately.'),
'G-MEM-05':('rejected','refuted by cleanup reproduction','When dyn_ex succeeds and dyn_ez fails, dyn_ex remains owned in w.dyn_ex and is freed at worker exit. One fixture with allocation35 failed returns-3 and tracked live bytes after nb_free are0. A two-fixture reuse crash is G-MEM-01, not an orphaned allocation.','No separate leak fix; use the G-MEM-01 failure-safe growth fix.'),
'G-FFI-04':('accepted','P3 API footgun','Dropping an unmanaged Batch makes it collectible but leaves48,956 requested native bytes. Explicit nb_free releases them. Inspected production callers use context-manager or finally cleanup.','Consider ffi.gc or weakref.finalize with close detachment if unmanaged use is supported; preserve explicit ownership.'),
'G-FFI-02':('unresolved','metric naming; no coverage defect verified','Fixture has2 discovered Strongholds but1 selected dynamic center; receipt anchors=1. Dynamic anchors are evaluated centers, unlike origin mode. Compact early rejects deliberately skip discovery. Substituting discovery.n changes the metric and does not measure all discovered Strongholds without additional expensive work.','Specify whether discovered_anchors means nominated centers or Stronghold inventory. Rename/document it rather than blindly switching the counter.'),
'G-FFI-05':('rejected','representation choice','All five Nether families are required by the prefix check and169 retained IDs/coordinates reconstruct witnesses. Missing redundant mask/first-witness fields does not establish lost evidence.','No ABI expansion justified.'),
'G-STORE-06':('rejected','operational risk; no production defect verified','A deliberately held external SQLite reader can prevent WAL reclamation: normal SQLite behavior. Production iterators fetch bounded pages before yielding. No leaked production reader was identified. TRUNCATE on close cannot overcome an active reader and may block.','Retain normal bounded-reader discipline; monitor WAL if this operational hypothesis arises.'),
'G-STORE-07':('rejected','refuted as present thread-confinement violation','Independent reproduction successfully runs prepare_range off-thread without touching db. A deliberately injected get_state off-thread correctly raises ProgrammingError. Future accidental SQL use is a maintainability concern, not an existing violation.','Keep SQLite thread checks and writer confinement; no check_same_thread=False change.'),
'G-STORE-08':('unresolved','hypothesis','Substring checks show unlocked cache access but no harmful interleaving, iteration exception, or wrong-result trace. The current CPython GIL protects individual dict operations; that alone does not prove compound behavior correct, either.','Provide a deterministic observable failure before prescribing synchronization.'),
'P-PERF-01':('accepted','measured optimization; updated by Sol','Lazy initialization is still unapplied and passes parity. Gemini verification script does not time throughput; its+10% repeats the historical result. Sol provides new matched-PGO screens and five-pair confirmation, including interaction with unused surface initialization.','Use Sol measured patch and adoption prerequisites; do not publish historical numbers as a new benchmark.')}
rows=[]
for r in source:
 d,severity,reason,action=D[r['id']]
 rows.append(dict(id=r['id'],original_severity=r['severity'],claim=r['title'],disposition=d,
                  reviewed_severity=severity,reason=reason,action=action,
                  source_file=r['file'],source_anchor_reference=r.get('anchor'),
                  evidence=['codex/reproductions.json',r['probe']]))
(base/'codex/dispositions.json').write_text(json.dumps(rows,indent=2)+'\n')
print('Wrote',len(rows),'reviewed Gemini dispositions.')
